 a size just below your main pack. Packs larger than this threshold are kept during `git gc`, effectively protecting the user's main pack. Caveat: if the number of kept packs exceeds `gc.autoPackLimit`, the threshold is ignored and all packs are consolidated.\n\n4. **Manual with `pack-objects --stdin-packs`:** List only promisor packs as input, exclude non-promisor packs with `^` prefix. Fully surgical but you'd need to manage the MIDX/cleanup yourself.\n\n5. **Incremental-repack via MIDX:** The most practical approach -- `git multi-pack-index repack --batch-size=<size>` will select only small packs to consolidate. If the user's main pack is large, it stays untouched naturally.\n\n## 6. Configuration Options That Control GC During Fetch\n\n| Config | Default | Effect |\n|--------|---------|--------|\n| `gc.auto` | 6700 | Number of loose objects before `gc --auto` triggers. **Set to 0 to disable all auto-gc**, including pack consolidation. |\n| `gc.autoPackLimit` | 50 | Number of non-`.keep` packs before `gc --auto` consolidates them. Set to 0 to disable pack consolidation trigger. |\n| `gc.bigPackThreshold` | 0 (disabled) | Packs larger than this are kept during gc. Overridden if kept packs exceed `gc.autoPackLimit`. |\n| `maintenance.auto` | true | Controls whether commands like `fetch` run `git maintenance run --auto` at the end. Set to `false` to disable. |\n| `fetch.writeCommitGraph` | false | If true, writes a commit-graph after fetching. Separate from gc. |\n| `gc.writeCommitGraph` | true | If true, gc rewrites the commit-graph when it runs. |\n| `maintenance.incremental-repack.auto` | 10 | Number of packs not in the MIDX before incremental-repack auto-triggers. |\n| `maintenance.strategy` | (none, or `geometric` for manual) | Can be `incremental` (avoids gc task entirely) or `geometric`. |\n\n**Most targeted approach for your case:**\n```bash\ngit -c gc.auto=0 fetch ...\n# or\ngit fetch --no-auto-gc ...\n```\n\n## 7. `--no-auto-gc` as a Fetch Flag\n\n**Yes, `--no-auto-gc` exists as a direct `git fetch` flag.** It is documented in `fetch-options`:\n\n> `--[no-]auto-maintenance`, `--[no-]auto-gc`: Run `git maintenance run --auto` at the end to perform automatic repository maintenance if needed. `--[no-]auto-gc` is a synonym. This is enabled by default.\n\nSo both of these are valid:\n```bash\ngit fetch --no-auto-gc\ngit fetch --no-auto-maintenance\n```\n\nThey are synonyms. `--no-auto-maintenance` is the newer name; `--no-auto-gc` is kept for backward compatibility.\n\nThe alternative config-based approach (`-c gc.auto=0`) is broader -- it disables gc triggers globally for that command invocation, including any internal gc heuristics. The `--no-auto-gc` flag specifically prevents the `git maintenance run --auto` call at the end of fetch.\n\n---\n\n## Practical Recommendations for Your Filtered-Fetch Scenario\n\nGiven that you're doing filtered fetches that create promisor packs and want to avoid triggering full gc on the user's repo:\n\n1. **Suppress auto-gc on fetch:** Use `git fetch --no-auto-gc` (or `--no-auto-maintenance`). This is the simplest and most direct approach.\n\n2. **If pack accumulation becomes a problem:** Use `git multi-pack-index write` after fetches to keep lookups fast without repacking. This is cheap and non-destructive.\n\n3. **If you need to consolidate accumulated promisor packs:** Use `git multi-pack-index repack --batch-size=<size>` which only touches small packs and leaves the user's main pack untouched. Or use `git repack --geometric=2 -d` which achieves the same via the geometric progression (only rolling up small packs).\n\n4. **If you want background maintenance without gc:** Set `maintenance.strategy=incremental` which schedules incremental-repack instead of gc. But this changes the user's repo config, which you probably don't want.\n\n5. **Nuclear option for protecting user packs:** Place `.keep` files on non-promisor packs, then `git repack -a -d` will only consolidate promisor packs. Remove `.keep` files when done.\n\nSources:\n- [Git - git-repack Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-repack)\n- [Git - git-gc Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-gc)\n- [Git - git-pack-objects Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-pack-objects)\n- [Git - git-maintenance Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-maintenance)\n- [Git - multi-pack-index Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/multi-pack-index)\n- [Git - git-multi-pack-index Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-multi-pack-index)\n- [Git - fetch-options Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/fetch-options)\n- [Git - partial-clone Documentation](https://git-scm.com/docs/partial-clone)\n- [Multi-Pack-Index (MIDX) Design Notes](https://www.kernel.org/pub//software/scm/git/docs/technical/multi-pack-index.html)\n- [Partial Clone Design Notes](https://www.kernel.org/pub/software/scm/git/docs/technical/partial-clone.html)\n- [maintenance: add incremental-repack task (patchwork)](https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/git/patch/00f47c48484c16987592d8b39fbd70e2744e3d4a.1596147867.git.gitgitgadget@gmail.com/)\n- [maintenance: add incremental-repack auto condition](https://github.com/git/git/commit/e841a79a131d8ce491cf04d0ca3e24f139a10b82)\n- [maintenance: auto-size incremental-repack batch](https://github.com/git/git/commit/a13e3d0ec87c9d12b93700375fceacdfb2c6885f)\n- [repack: add --filter=\\<filter-spec\\> option (patchwork)](https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/git/patch/20230812000011.1227371-6-christian.couder@gmail.com/)"}],"totalDurationMs":1080700,"totalTokens":41017,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":36479,"output_tokens":3647,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":890},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3647,"cache_read_input_tokens":36479,"cache